<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Diffusion models learn intermediate representations that support semantic
segmentation, image classification, and semantic correspondence
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Baranchuk et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiang et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. Using these representations for a
downstream task requires choosing which activations to extract. The available
features depend on the denoising timestep and network layer, and each feature
map contains a set of channels from which the task representation is formed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Existing methods address this choice through fixed extraction rules, learned
aggregation across timesteps and layers, or timestep selection during
distillation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang and Wang, 2023</a>)</cite>. RepFusion transfers features from a
frozen diffusion teacher to a student and learns which timestep to use. This
leaves the choice of layer and retained feature dimensions as further parts
of the extraction problem. These choices also determine which activations
must be stored and used as distillation targets.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Policy-Mask</span> selects a timestep, a layer, and a channel subset under a
prescribed channel budget. The policy takes the input image and budget and
selects an action <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=(t,l,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=(t,l,K)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|K|=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|K|=b</annotation></semantics></math>. A task decoder provides the
selection reward, and the selected features supervise the student during
training. At inference, the student processes the image without evaluating
the diffusion teacher. This extends RepFusion’s timestep selection to a joint
choice of extraction point and feature subset.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our contributions are:</p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A budgeted <math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,l,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,l,K)</annotation></semantics></math> policy with exact-cardinality sampling.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A channel-score normalization that controls the relative action-head contributions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At 128 of 1280 aligned channels, gains of 1.2–1.6 mIoU over full-width
fixed extraction on four segmentation benchmarks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A formal action mapping from U-Net features to DiT, MMDiT, and flow
transformer feature lattices.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#S2" title="2 Related work ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reviews related work, Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Method ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>
defines the policy, Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> reports experiments, and
Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Conclusion ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> concludes. Appendices <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>–<a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Qualitative and class-wise analysis ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>
provide experimental details and additional results.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Related work</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diffusion representations.</span>
Diffusion features support dense prediction, correspondence, segmentation, and
depth estimation through task-specific extraction rules
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Baranchuk et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiang et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang and Wang, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ji et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ke et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Recent work studies prompt selection,
noise-free representations, and the transfer of stable diffusion to dense
tasks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tian et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kondapaneni et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Stracke et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ravishankar et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. RepFusion is the closest predecessor: it
distills a recognizer from a frozen diffusion teacher after selecting a useful
noise step <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang and Wang, 2023</a>)</cite>. <span id="S2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Policy-Mask</span> keeps the same teacher–student
division and expands the selected object to <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,l,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,l,K)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Budgeted subset selection.</span>
Feature selection spans filters, wrappers, continuous relaxations, and greedy
methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al., 2005</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kohavi and John, 1997</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abid et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Das and Kempe, 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Elenberg et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mirzasoleiman et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nemhauser et al., 1978</a>)</cite>. <span id="S2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Policy-Mask</span> selects feature dimensions of one frozen model response.
Budget-conditioned policies also appear in diffusion caching, where ReCache
selects recomputation steps under an inference budget <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aliev et al., 2026</a>)</cite>.
Here the budget constrains feature coordinates used for distillation.
The policy uses a Plackett–Luce ordering and a Gumbel top-<math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> sampler
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Plackett, 1975</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kool et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. Its gradient estimator follows the standard
score-function construction with a baseline <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Greensmith et al., 2004</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kool et al., 2020</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Method</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Policy-Mask</span> learns which teacher response to distill under an exact channel
budget. The task decoder evaluates the selected response, and its loss supplies
the policy reward while the selected feature supervises the student.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Problem setup</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be a data distribution over <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and let the frozen
teacher <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> expose <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t,l}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{C_{t,l}\times H_{t,l}\times W_{t,l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t,l}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{C_{t,l}\times H_{t,l}\times W_{t,l}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
An alignment map <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> projects a candidate layer to a common feature space,
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t,l}(x)=A_{l}(F_{t,l}(x))\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times H_{s}\times W_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t,l}(x)=A_{l}(F_{t,l}(x))\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times H_{s}\times W_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This makes a
single exact budget meaningful even when raw layers have different widths and
resolutions. In the ADE20K experiments with trainable <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, the KD loss fell below
0.005 within two epochs. We therefore fixed <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> at initialization for the
normalization ablation and the RepFusion comparison.
Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Fixed alignment ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> provides the experimental details. During training, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is queried, or its responses are drawn
from a feature bank. At inference, the student alone consumes <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang and Wang, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
For budget <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, the feasible action set is:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{b}=\{(t,l,K):t\in\mathcal{T},\ l\in\mathcal{L},\ K\subseteq[C],\ |K|=b\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{b}=\{(t,l,K):t\in\mathcal{T},\ l\in\mathcal{L},\ K\subseteq[C],\ |K|=b\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">With a binary channel mask <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, the selected response is
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{F}_{a}(x)=G_{t,l}(x)\odot m_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{F}_{a}(x)=G_{t,l}(x)\odot m_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. The student returns task logits
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\phi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\phi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and a projected feature <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and is trained with:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm stu}=\ell_{\rm task}(u_{\phi}(x),y)+\lambda\ell_{\rm KD}\!\left(p_{\phi}(x),\operatorname{sg}[\widetilde{F}_{a}(x)]\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>stu</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>KD</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm stu}=\ell_{\rm task}(u_{\phi}(x),y)+\lambda\ell_{\rm KD}\!\left(p_{\phi}(x),\operatorname{sg}[\widetilde{F}_{a}(x)]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{sg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>sg</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{sg}</annotation></semantics></math> stops gradients through the frozen target. A small
task decoder <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math> maps the selected teacher feature to task predictions. Holding
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> fixed during a policy step, the selector objective is:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J_{b}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D},\ a\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\,|\,x,b)}\left[-\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}\!\left(q_{\omega}(\widetilde{F}_{a}(x)),y\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>dec</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{b}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D},\ a\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\,|\,x,b)}\left[-\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}\!\left(q_{\omega}(\widetilde{F}_{a}(x)),y\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2610.28889v1/fig_method.png" id="S3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/284;" width="548" height="284" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span><span id="S3.F1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Policy-Mask</span> training and inference. Given an image <math id="S3.F1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and a budget
<math id="S3.F1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, the policy <math id="S3.F1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> outputs distributions over timesteps and layers
and channel logits <math id="S3.F1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>. A timestep <math id="S3.F1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and a layer <math id="S3.F1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> are sampled.
An ordered sequence <math id="S3.F1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\sim\pi_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\sim\pi_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.F1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> channels is drawn without
replacement by Gumbel top-<math id="S3.F1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, giving the mask <math id="S3.F1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. The frozen diffusion model <math id="S3.F1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>
returns <math id="S3.F1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t,l}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t,l}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> after the alignment <math id="S3.F1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, and masking gives
<math id="S3.F1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{F}_{a}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{F}_{a}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. This feature is the distillation target for the student
<math id="S3.F1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> and, through the task decoder <math id="S3.F1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives the reward
<math id="S3.F1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=-\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>dec</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=-\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The policy is updated by REINFORCE with baseline <math id="S3.F1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>
and the channel score scaled by <math id="S3.F1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/b</annotation></semantics></math> (Equation <a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.3 Channel-score normalization ‣ 3 Method ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). At inference, only
<math id="S3.F1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is evaluated. Images and predictions are ADE20K validation examples
(Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.4 Transformer teachers ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Both <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rm task}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rm task}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>dec</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}</annotation></semantics></math> use the training annotation <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>:
pixel-wise supervision for segmentation, cross-entropy for classification, and
the corresponding matching loss. On ADE20K, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>dec</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}</annotation></semantics></math> averages
cross-entropy over valid pixels per image. The student task loss also includes
Dice loss.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The policy therefore receives one scalar reward
per sampled action, while held-out mIoU, top-1 accuracy, and PCK remain
evaluation metrics. The teacher is not differentiated through.
The action is discrete, and the feasible set has
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{A}_{b}|=|\mathcal{T}|\,|\mathcal{L}|\binom{C}{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>C</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{A}_{b}|=|\mathcal{T}|\,|\mathcal{L}|\binom{C}{b}</annotation></semantics></math> elements.
Rather than enumerating subsets, we sample actions and use a policy gradient.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Policy over budgeted subsets</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The policy samples an ordered index sequence
<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=(k_{1},\ldots,k_{b})\in\operatorname{Perm}_{b}([C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Perm</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=(k_{1},\ldots,k_{b})\in\operatorname{Perm}_{b}([C])</annotation></semantics></math> and then uses the
unordered set <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(\sigma)=\{k_{1},\ldots,k_{b}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(\sigma)=\{k_{1},\ldots,k_{b}\}</annotation></semantics></math> to form the mask. It factorizes as:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(t,l,\sigma\,|\,x,b)=\pi_{t}(t\,|\,x,b)\,\pi_{l}(l\,|\,x,b)\,\pi_{\sigma}(\sigma\,|\,x,b)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(t,l,\sigma\,|\,x,b)=\pi_{t}(t\,|\,x,b)\,\pi_{l}(l\,|\,x,b)\,\pi_{\sigma}(\sigma\,|\,x,b).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The first two factors are categorical. For channel logits <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, we draw
independent Gumbel perturbations and take the <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> largest perturbed logits
in descending order:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{c}=-\log(-\log U_{c}),\quad U_{c}\overset{\rm iid}{\sim}\operatorname{Uniform}(0,1),\qquad\sigma=\operatorname{Top}_{b}(z+g)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">iid</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Top</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{c}=-\log(-\log U_{c}),\quad U_{c}\overset{\rm iid}{\sim}\operatorname{Uniform}(0,1),\qquad\sigma=\operatorname{Top}_{b}(z+g).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This produces an ordered draw <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{1},\ldots,k_{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{1},\ldots,k_{b})</annotation></semantics></math> without replacement. Its
exact Plackett–Luce score is:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\pi_{\sigma}(\sigma\,|\,x,b)=\sum_{j=1}^{b}\left[z_{k_{j}}-\log\!\!\sum_{c\notin\{k_{1},\ldots,k_{j-1}\}}\!\!\exp z_{c}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:1.143em;" width="1.143em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>exp</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\sigma}(\sigma\,|\,x,b)=\sum_{j=1}^{b}\left[z_{k_{j}}-\log\!\!\sum_{c\notin\{k_{1},\ldots,k_{j-1}\}}\!\!\exp z_{c}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The reward is invariant to the order of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, but the score is evaluated
on the draw that generated the mask. Top-<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> therefore returns <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> distinct
coordinates with exact feasibility rather than a sparsity penalty. Holding the
decoder fixed, an action-independent baseline <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> gives the score-function
estimator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Greensmith et al., 2004</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kool et al., 2020</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{g}=(R-c)\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(t,l,\sigma\,|\,x,b),\qquad\mathbb{E}[\widehat{g}]=\nabla_{\theta}J_{b}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}=(R-c)\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(t,l,\sigma\,|\,x,b),\qquad\mathbb{E}[\widehat{g}]=\nabla_{\theta}J_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Policy-Mask</span>: training and task inference</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            frozen teacher <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, student <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, task decoder <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, policy <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, budget <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each minibatch <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
              sample <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,l,\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,l,\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x,b)</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leftarrow K(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leftarrow K(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{F}\leftarrow A_{l}(F_{t,l}^{D}(x))\odot m_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{F}\leftarrow A_{l}(F_{t,l}^{D}(x))\odot m_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leftarrow-\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}(q_{\omega}(\widetilde{F}),y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>dec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leftarrow-\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}(q_{\omega}(\widetilde{F}),y)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              update <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R-c)\nabla_{\theta}[\log\pi_{t}+\log\pi_{l}+b^{-1}\log\pi_{\sigma}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R-c)\nabla_{\theta}[\log\pi_{t}+\log\pi_{l}+b^{-1}\log\pi_{\sigma}]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              update <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm stu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>stu</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm stu}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg1.l7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}(q_{\omega}(\operatorname{sg}[\widetilde{F}]),y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>dec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}(q_{\omega}(\operatorname{sg}[\widetilde{F}]),y)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inference:</span> return <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\phi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\phi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> without evaluating <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The implementation uses a stopped moving baseline for variance reduction. The task decoder supplies <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=-\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>dec</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=-\ell_{\mathrm{dec}}</annotation></semantics></math> and is trained on the same
decoder loss with its input detached. This separates selection from the student’s
task and distillation losses. Emitting action logits costs
<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(|\mathcal{T}|+|\mathcal{L}|+C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|\mathcal{T}|+|\mathcal{L}|+C)</annotation></semantics></math>, and Gumbel perturbation plus top-<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>
selection is linear in <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> up to the partial-sort cost. A frozen teacher query
and layer alignment dominate these selector operations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Channel-score normalization</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The channel score in Equation <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.2 Policy over budgeted subsets ‣ 3 Method ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> is a sum of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> terms, whereas the
timestep and layer scores each contain one term. Dividing the channel score
by <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> replaces this sum with its mean and controls its relative weight in
the joint update. It does not assume that gradient norms grow linearly with
<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. We use:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\rm bal}=(R-c)\nabla_{\theta}\left[\log\pi_{t}+\log\pi_{l}+\frac{1}{b}\log\pi_{\sigma}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>bal</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\rm bal}=(R-c)\nabla_{\theta}\left[\log\pi_{t}+\log\pi_{l}+\frac{1}{b}\log\pi_{\sigma}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/b</annotation></semantics></math> factor is a preconditioner, so the controlled update is not claimed
to be an unbiased estimator of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}J_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}J_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. For disjoint heads and
plain SGD, it is equivalent to reducing only the channel-head
learning rate by <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. With a shared trunk, adaptive moments, and entropy
regularization, it instead changes the relative head contribution
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2018</a>)</cite>. The action-axis ablation motivates this control: the
unnormalized joint policy reaches 31.68 mIoU, compared with 31.78 for the
timestep-only policy (Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.4 Transformer teachers ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). With fixed alignment,
normalization raises mean best-validation mIoU from 36.8 to 37.7 over three
seeds (Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Additional results ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental setup</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Teacher and student.</span>
The main selector comparisons use a frozen SD-1.5 U-Net and a common width
of 1280 aligned channels. Compact selectors retain 128 channels. The student
loss and updates are given in Equation <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.1 Problem setup ‣ 3 Method ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and
Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.2 Policy over budgeted subsets ‣ 3 Method ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets and metrics.</span>
Segmentation is evaluated on ADE20K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, Cityscapes
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cordts et al., 2016</a>)</cite>, CelebA-HQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, and Pascal VOC
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Everingham et al., 2010</a>)</cite> using mIoU. Classification uses CIFAR-10 and
CIFAR-100 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Krizhevsky, 2009</a>)</cite> top-1 accuracy. Semantic correspondence uses
SPair-71k <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Min et al., 2019</a>)</cite>
PCK@0.1 with image and bounding-box normalization reported separately.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span>
The baselines include fixed extraction, top-variance and Fisher channel
selection, and full-width extraction. The DDAE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiang et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and
RepFusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang and Wang, 2023</a>)</cite> entries in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 Main results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> retain
their corresponding source protocols.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Main results</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At 128 selected channels, <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Policy-Mask</span> exceeds full-width extraction at a fixed
<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,l)</annotation></semantics></math> by 1.5, 1.6, 1.2, and 1.3 mIoU on ADE20K, Cityscapes, CelebA-HQ,
and Pascal VOC, respectively (Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.2 Main results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). These results
compare feature-selection rules at 10% of the full aligned width.</p>
