</figure>
<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We transfer the action to teachers with an ordered feature lattice. A U-Net
teacher <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ronneberger et al., 2015</a>)</cite> uses denoising steps, layers, and channels. For
a DiT, MMDiT, or flow transformer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peebles and Xie, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Esser et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lipman et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, let
<math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\rm img}_{\lambda,d}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>img</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\rm img}_{\lambda,d}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the image-token state at
log-SNR or flow coordinate <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and depth <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding selected
target is:</p>
