<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Channel-budget sweep</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4.4 Transformer teachers ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Policy-Mask: Budget-Aware Adaptation of Diffusion Features to Discriminative Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> compares channel budgets on ADE20K using
top-magnitude selection at a fixed timestep and layer, with a separate student
trained for each budget. The highest validation mIoU is obtained at <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=256</annotation></semantics></math>.
The masked distillation loss is averaged over all 1280 channels, so changing
the budget also changes its scale. This experiment does not isolate the effect
of channel count from the change in distillation strength.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Fixed alignment</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With trainable <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, the KD loss fell below 0.005 within two epochs in each
diagnostic run. This behavior is consistent with projection shrinkage toward
zero. We therefore fixed <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for the channel-score normalization ablation
and the RepFusion comparison.</p>
</div>
</section>
